  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Mangaluru?", answer: "Share your child's programme or board, subject, level and exam series with IB Gram, and we shortlist tutors who teach that exact course. Since only three Mangaluru schools run Cambridge IGCSE and none run the IB Diploma, matching is based on syllabus fit rather than location. A free trial lesson comes before any decision, and we suggest another tutor if the match is not right." },
    { question: "Which schools in Mangaluru offer IGCSE?", answer: "Three schools currently run Cambridge IGCSE: The Bharath Academy on Yeyyadi Road, TLC Cambridge International School at the CFAL campus in Kavoor, and The Cambridge International School near Adyar, which also runs CBSE. Canara International School and the Early Learning Centre follow Cambridge Primary and Lower Secondary but stop before IGCSE." },
    { question: "Is there an IB school in Mangaluru?", answer: "No. No school in Mangaluru currently offers the IB Primary Years, Middle Years or Diploma Programme. Families who want the IB study through an online or out-of-state provider and add subject-specific tutoring, or they look toward Bengaluru, which has several established IB World Schools." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Mangaluru for Edexcel as well as Cambridge?", answer: "We can match Edexcel IGCSE tutors for a Mangaluru family, though it is worth knowing that none of the city's schools currently run the Edexcel specification themselves; the local market is Cambridge-only. Most Mangaluru requests are for Cambridge subjects and tiers, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for example, matched against current CAIE past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Mangaluru?", answer: "No. In-person home tuition is limited to Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; everywhere else, Mangaluru included, a lesson is live video with a shared digital whiteboard, one to one. This is genuine online private tuition delivered to your home over a screen, not a promise that a tutor rings the doorbell." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Mangaluru cost?", answer: "The fee depends on the programme and level, the subject, session length and how recently a tutor has taught that exact syllabus, and it is confirmed for your specific match before the trial. An IB Diploma HL subject usually costs more than Cambridge IGCSE Core work, since fewer tutors nationally teach it. No travel cost is ever added, since every lesson is online, and there is no long contract." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before I commit?", answer: "Yes. Every match opens with a free trial lesson where your child works through a real topic from their own syllabus with the tutor, at no cost and with no obligation to continue. The tutor then shares a short first-month plan, and you decide whether to proceed, ask for changes, or try someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments from Mangaluru?", answer: "Yes, though never by writing any part of it. Genuine help covers choosing a workable research question, explaining what each assessment criterion actually rewards, planning data collection, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting assessed work breaches IB academic integrity rules, and IB Gram tutors decline those requests outright." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with from Mangaluru?", answer: "We cover the subject groups most requested by Diploma students studying from Mangaluru: Maths Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, alongside Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students in Mangaluru, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, across the full continuum. MYP support usually focuses on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and Language and Literature, plus the Personal Project's process journal, often for a student bridging into one of the city's Cambridge IGCSE schools. PYP support covers reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research skills." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Mangaluru?", answer: "It works well here, especially given how few local specialists exist outside the city's three Cambridge schools. A shared digital whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked solutions cover most of what a tutor sitting beside your child would otherwise do, while opening up specialists across India rather than a handful locally." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Mangaluru students?", answer: "Every tutor is checked on qualifications, recent teaching experience with the exact subject and level, and their approach to assessment criteria before meeting any family. Given how small Mangaluru's local IB and IGCSE base is, we specifically look for tutors who have taught that syllabus recently elsewhere in India. The free trial lesson then lets you judge the fit directly." },
    { question: "When should my child in Mangaluru start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally at the start of the course, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, giving time to build foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades arrive. Starting in the final year can still help meaningfully, with tutoring focused on the highest-value topics and past papers before the exam series." },
    { question: "My child is switching from CBSE, ICSE or Karnataka's SSLC to IGCSE in Mangaluru. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, this comes up often, particularly around the move into one of the city's three Cambridge schools at Grade 9. The main gap is usually question style, not content: IGCSE's command words and mark-scheme expectations differ from what a CBSE, ICSE or SSLC paper rewards, and that needs explicit teaching, ideally starting before the switch itself." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Mangaluru?", answer: "Yes, most families book weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings. We plan around Mangaluru's June-to-September monsoon, when connectivity can be less reliable on the heaviest rain days, and build in some flexibility around that. Adding a second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is straightforward online." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Mangaluru?", answer: "Tell us, and we will find someone else. Progress is reviewed with families every few weeks, and we re-match whenever the fit is wrong rather than asking a child to persist with someone who is not working. There are no long contracts, so pausing or stopping carries no penalty." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Mangaluru school, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram operates independently, with no affiliation to or endorsement from any Mangaluru school, the International Baccalaureate Organization or Cambridge Assessment International Education. School names on this page describe the city's genuine, limited Cambridge landscape, and tutors work to each student's own syllabus and exam calendar." },
    { question: "My family is moving to Mangaluru and my child needs to continue their IB Diploma. Can you help?", answer: "Yes, and this is a fairly common situation given how many families relocate here for shipping, refining, IT or healthcare work. Since no school in Mangaluru runs the Diploma, we match a tutor who has taught the identical HL and SL subjects at the same stage, so your child can keep pace with an online or out-of-state provider without losing time to the move." },
  ],

